{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1468559-ideas-for-time-4-trigger-spells","id":1468559,"title":"Ideas for Time 4 trigger spells","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2021-11-21T20:54:20-08:00","id":1468559,"title":"Ideas for Time 4 trigger spells","content":"So, I'd like to see ideafor a Life 3, Forces 3, Prime 1 Hermetic mage that gets gis hand into a Time 4 sonder that can &quot;trap&quot; spells to trigger later as the Time 4 effect we know. I thought about some examples:<br /> <br /> 1- Life 3 buffs with good rolls to instantly buff when needed triggered by a specific sound effect (a particular whistle?) with Forces<br /> <br /> 2- Life effect to heal you whenever your jealth drops to woumded or lower, triggered by Life. Could you be healed more than once with a single spell trapped? Like, drop to wounded, heal, drop to wounded, heal again?<br /> <br /> 3- Life 3/Forces 3 to turn into an element when you make a specific sound or your health get to crippled or lower (Forces/Life trigger), so you can get the hell away from dangerous situations.<br /> <br /> 4- A Forces 3 paralyze spell, also triggered by Forces (sound), to stop someone from doing something you don't want.<br /> <br /> 5- Big ass fireball or lightning with lots of successes to blow everything in case you need it.<br /> <br /> 6- Maybe a Forces shield too when you get some damage?<br /> <br /> I can only think in combat or dangerous sotuations spells, would love to see more mundane and useful examples, like:<br /> <br /> 7- Maybe a Forces 3 spell to turn off all electricity in an area, pretty much like a big EMP device...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3153-lord-revan","name":"Lord Revan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3153_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-21T22:11:02-08:00","id":1468562,"title":"","content":"#3 is the best choice. Survive the encounter.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thank you for passing time with me in conversation. <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1480242-horizon-s-wild-and-crazy-homebrew-rules-and-metaplot-choices\" target=\"_blank\">My Hacks</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26467-horizonparty2021","name":"HorizonParty2021","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26467_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"610"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-22T10:29:56-08:00","id":1468602,"title":"","content":"Your main advantages with triggered spells is building up successes in advance and casting in a favorable location (such as away from prying eyes). Your mundane examples are going to need to involve one of those, most likely the former. If you have a very attention grabbing paradigm, though, the latter will come into play as well.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-22T12:19:26-08:00","id":1468618,"title":"","content":"You can't repeat the same casting of Life again and again to keep healing, unless that's specifically what the wonder does. By itself the trigger will hold a single casting.<br /> <br /> That said, you can think of a ritual with Life that uses a lot of successes to have a big regeneration pool or something like that.<br /> <br /> \u200bAs <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar758_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"758\" data-vbnamecard=\"758\">Ramnesis</a> said, your biggest pay from this wonder will come from effects that benefit from as many successes as possible. Either complex spells or very potent effects.<br /> <br /> So for combat it is actually of limited use. You'll have a spell with big oomph, but a single use, so it would have to be a key casting. Instead, think about a few specific effects that would benefit from a big amount of successes, but that you would want to cast out of your own base.<br /> <br /> From the ideas you presented, I think your best choices would be either the healing effect or the elemental transformation, but both using large pools of successes to make them as versatile and useful as possible.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-23T04:55:50-08:00","id":1468675,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1468559-ideas-for-time-4-trigger-spells?p=1468618#post1468618\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You can't repeat the same casting of Life again and again to keep healing, unless that's specifically what the wonder does. By itself the trigger will hold a single casting.<br /> <br /> That said, you can think of a ritual with Life that uses a lot of successes to have a big regeneration pool or something like that.</div> </div> </div> </div>A healing pool is a good idea.<br /> <br /> \u200b<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1468559-ideas-for-time-4-trigger-spells?p=1468618#post1468618\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar758_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"758\" data-vbnamecard=\"758\">Ramnesis</a> said, your biggest pay from this wonder will come from effects that benefit from as many successes as possible. Either complex spells or very potent effects.<br /> <br /> So for combat it is actually of limited use. You'll have a spell with big oomph, but a single use, so it would have to be a key casting. Instead, think about a few specific effects that would benefit from a big amount of successes, but that you would want to cast out of your own base.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes. That's why I thought about defenses in very dangerous situations. The combat one was the big ass fireball that you won't use all the time. Just when you feel the need to blow everything up.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1468559-ideas-for-time-4-trigger-spells?p=1468618#post1468618\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">From the ideas you presented, I think your best choices would be either the healing effect or the elemental transformation, but both using large pools of successes to make them as versatile and useful as possible.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, definitely. I was thinking about making a strng force shield instead of healing (or both?) It is less dangerous to protect health than to heal after being hit.<br /> <br /> Do you guys have other examples, maybe something you've done in a game?<br /> <br /> <br /> EDIT: How would the healing work if the trigger is &quot;if hp goes in apacitsded or worse&quot;? What if you get 8 of more damage, instantly killing you, would the trigger act quick enough to heal? Since it's a Time 4 effect, I can see the vealing being activated the precise moment that the body takes such damage and hrals before killing the mage...<br /> <br /> Also:<br /> <br /> 8- Placing traps in a area that trigger when someone (or even a specific person) engers it. The trap could be a Life &quot;sleeping&quot; spell or s Forces damage or paralyze.<br /> Although, I don't know if this really requires Time 4 or it can be done just with Life/Forces. Since the area is not moving, there's no need for locking the effect.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3153,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3153-lord-revan","user":"Lord Revan","date":". 11-23-2021, 08:11 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3153-lord-revan","name":"Lord Revan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3153_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-24T04:28:20-08:00","id":1468741,"title":"","content":"The problem with a healing or defensive effect is just to think about why you would need to cast it on the fly. The same for a trap. You can always cast those things on yourself at home before leaving.<br /> <br /> And the problem with timing the healing to a certain point in your Health Track is that I'm not sure if it really can save you from death as you want. At least not only due to the Time 4 trigger.<br /> <br /> Remember that a wonder is limited to its own specific effect. You don't have access to Time 4, you have access to a spell trigger. If that effect alone isn't enough, forget it. That's also why you have to specify your entire spell before storing it.<br /> <br /> I think your best bet is the Elemental Body because it is versatile. Lets say you make a light body and store it. With a huge amount of successes, you give this body flight, safe travel modes, a number of energy senses and so on. You can use the light body later to escape, reach hard places, scout, heat things up, send messages, etc. You have only one stored effect, but you make this effect the most versatile possible.<br /> <br /> You should think along those lines to make a small pool of regular uses, spells that give you the most different uses for your casting, taking full advantage of a big number of successes. You could make the transformation into elemental body start by healing you, and trigger that by taking damage, or damage from a source with at least 8 dice of damage.<br /> <br /> But you'll probably find more uses in game, because most spells that will really benefit from this combination: casting it with many successes at home, trigger at another place, will be spells strategically chosen to deal with your current goals in game.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-24T07:11:41-08:00","id":1468755,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1468559-ideas-for-time-4-trigger-spells?p=1468741#post1468741\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The problem with a healing or defensive effect is just to think about why you would need to cast it on the fly. The same for a trap. You can always cast those things on yourself at home before leaving.</div> </div> </div> </div>The healing on the fly is for the case of getting too much damage too quickly. And to avoid death. But this could be done by the elementsl body indeed. Then the only reason would be to not waste a turn healing. And a good healing guaranteed.<br /> You're right about the traps. The obly advantage would be to get more successes, but if you're carefully placing a trap, then you probably have time to get enough successes, so Time 4 is indeed not needed.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1468559-ideas-for-time-4-trigger-spells?p=1468741#post1468741\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And the problem with timing the healing to a certain point in your Health Track is that I'm not sure if it really can save you from death as you want. At least not only due to the Time 4 trigger.</div> </div> </div> </div>That depends how quick the effect is released. A trigger inplies that it's very quick, like fractions of a second. That might be enough to avoid death, unless you're instantly vaporized by a nuke..<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1468559-ideas-for-time-4-trigger-spells?p=1468741#post1468741\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But you'll probably find more uses in game, because most spells that will really benefit from this combination: casting it with many successes at home, trigger at another place, will be spells strategically chosen to deal with your current goals in game.</div> </div> </div> </div>There is another advantage with trigger spells: they don't count as an Arete roll when triggered (and not even an action) and they act instantly. <br /> I wonder which good ideas this can create.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3153-lord-revan","name":"Lord Revan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3153_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-24T08:43:54-08:00","id":1468761,"title":"","content":"My reasoning with healing and defensive spells is that you can set them beforehand. Make a ritual before leaving home if you think this may come in handy, so you have already the effect on you.<br /> <br /> And the damage thing depends too much on how the ST will rule it. The crux of the matter is that, since it is a wonder with A Time 4 effect, and not actually The Time 4 Sphere, your ST have far more leeway in how to interpret it. It isn't your own Sphere no matter what, so you can't say how it will work, the ST did that.<br /> <br /> But talk with your group about ideas for trigger spells. They're the ones on the same chronicle, going through the same challenges, they're better suited to brainstorm useful ideas for your actual context.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-24T18:58:26-08:00","id":1468804,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1468559-ideas-for-time-4-trigger-spells?p=1468761#post1468761\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My reasoning with healing and defensive spells is that you can set them beforehand. Make a ritual before leaving home if you think this may come in handy, so you have already the effect on you.</div> </div> </div> </div>You mean an always running effect? That heals whenever hp goes wounded or lower?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3153-lord-revan","name":"Lord Revan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3153_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-25T03:11:03-08:00","id":1468823,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lord Revan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1468559-ideas-for-time-4-trigger-spells?p=1468804#post1468804\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You mean an always running effect? That heals whenever hp goes wounded or lower?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yup. You can do that with Life alone. Instead of applying a Time trigger, you just give yourself a regeneration factor with a pool of &quot;healing points&quot;. You'll just have to add successes for duration and, well, run around with an active spell, but that isn't that different from running around with a trigger-bound spell.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}